{
  "_readme": [
    "Single source of every preset colour. Edit here, then run: python3 scripts/build.py css",
    "Each preset has a dark and a light set. Optional keys: background, text, link, linkHover, codeTint.",
    "background: replaces the preview background. text: replaces the body text colour. link / linkHover: replace the VS Code link colours.",
    "codeTint: colour of the inline-code box (defaults to the code colour). Tints and borders are derived automatically. codeTintAlpha / codeBorderAlpha (0 to 1): opacity of the inline-code box and of an optional thin border. linkUnderline: true underlines every link; \"external\" underlines web and mail links only, other links on hover.",
    "Tables: tableBg (surface), tableHead (header text), tableBorder / tableHeadBorder (grid lines and the line under the header), tableBorderAlpha / tableHeadBorderAlpha (0 to 1), tableRadius (1 to 32 px, rounded outer edge), tableHeadBg / tableHeadBgAlpha (header row fill), tableHeadWeight (100 to 900). Without them, lines mix the text colour into the background.",
    "Links: linkBorder draws the underline as a bottom border (thicker on hover); linkWeight (100 to 900). Inline code: codeRadius (px), codePadding (for example \"2px 8px\").",
    "Code blocks (box only; syntax colours stay VS Code): preBg, preBorder, preBorderAlpha, preRadius, prePadding.",
    "Callouts for > [!NOTE] / [!INFO], > [!TIP] and > [!WARNING] quotes: alerts.note / tip / warning, each with text, bg, border and optional bgAlpha; alertRadius, alertPadding; alertIcon / alertIconGap (px): size of the Markdown All in One icon and the gap before the text."
  ],
